{"ratings":[{"id":"F1","consequence":"secret","trigger":"plausible","reason":"An unpublished ancestor or branch name containing private information can be pushed to the remote without the publication checks examining it."},{"id":"F2","consequence":"bypass","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A commit linking to another coordinator run can bypass the discreet-mode marker check when the worker uses a different UI address."},{"id":"F3","consequence":"boundary","trigger":"plausible","reason":"If the supplied token is rejected, Git may consult the owner's credential helper and authenticate with a different credential despite the intended token-only boundary."}]}